Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a theft and consequent water damage loss at our client's Kestrel Ridge Retail Center in Boise. Our reference is HV/RET/2025/9083.

I do not have the policy number to hand - the account renewed in January and the binder is with our Boise office - so please search on the property address and our reference. The owner entity is the Delaware limited partnership and Aspenwall Commercial Realty are the managing agent named on the policy.

Broker reference: HV/RET/2025/9083
Insured name: Kestrel Ridge Holdings, LP
Managing agent: Aspenwall Commercial Realty, LLC
Date of loss: 2 March 2026
Loss location: 4820 - 4890 North Eagle Ridge Boulevard, Boise, ID 83713
Cause: Theft of copper and consequent water damage
Estimated loss: USD 425,000

Someone forced the rear service door of a vacant in-line suite overnight on
Sunday and stripped copper out of the ceiling plenum. Cutting a live 2-inch
domestic line is what did the damage - it ran for somewhere between three and
six hours before the morning porter found it.

Three occupied suites and the rear corridor took water. One tenant is closed and
another is trading at reduced capacity. Boise PD attended and there is camera
footage of two individuals and a white pickup, which we have preserved.

Two suites in that run are vacant under the permit written into the policy at
renewal, and the weekly inspection log is available.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * restoration contractor's assessment
  * mitigation and reinstatement schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. Our client would like your
view on whether the theft deductible or the water damage deductible applies,
and whether the copper theft sublimit reaches the resulting water damage.

